cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the manuscript when using this result or its formalization."
title: "Sharp universal Rényi threshold for iid sums on finite Sidon sets"
authors:
  - family-names: Goyal
    given-names: Dev D.
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  For real orders alpha greater than one, uniform input maximizes the
  Renyi entropy of the sum of two iid draws on every nonempty finite strong Sidon
  support exactly when 2^(alpha-1) <= 2 alpha-1. The result includes the
  critical endpoint and zero input probabilities. Historical novelty
  of the matching universal sufficient bound remains provisional.
preferred-citation:
